    "body": "COLD_START_PROBE_V1\n\nThis is a non-production continuity proof. Assume the agent has ZERO prior chat/session context.\n\nDo not infer current project state from this issue body. Use this body only as the request to perform the probe.\n\nStart from repository `main`. Discover and obey the repository's native agent instructions. Reconstruct the durable continuity map using only repository/GitHub evidence.\n\nCreate exactly one documentation file: `docs/proofs/agent-restart-cold-start-v1.md`.\n\nThe report must include:\n- the repository instruction file(s) actually discovered and used;\n- exact main HEAD observed at start;\n- the current durable tracker/PR/workflow sources the instructions direct you to use;\n- Permanent Archive V1 workflow path, archive branch, archive root, and at least one verified archived event envelope/raw pointer;\n- whether any legacy snapshot disagrees with fresher GitHub evidence, without treating stale data as authoritative;\n- a final verdict `DURABLE_RESTART_CONTEXT = PROVEN` or `NOT_PROVEN`, with exact evidence references.\n\nRules:\n- docs-only; no source/config/workflow/state/canon mutation;\n- do not invent missing evidence;\n- do not rewrite archive history;\n- do not merge;\n- if context cannot be proven, say NOT_PROVEN and explain exactly what is missing.\n\nThe purpose is to prove that a fresh coding agent can recover context from GitHub without SPARX manually retelling prior work.",
